  "final_text": "I fixed the bug in `invoicing/currency.py`. `minor_units()` called `currency.lower()` and compared the result to `ZERO_DECIMAL`, which holds uppercase codes. \"JPY\" therefore never matched and was treated as a 2-decimal currency, so the total came out as `\u00a514,118.50`. I changed it to `currency.upper()`. `test_invoice_jpy` now passes, and so do the other 7 tests in the suite."
